# Finding paths around a cycle
#
# Three edges form a directed cycle. Recursive forward N3 rules derive
# reachable pairs, stopping when every consequence is already present.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/cyclic-reachability#> .

# The three one-way edges form a closed loop.
:a :edge :b .
:b :edge :c .
:c :edge :a .

# Every edge gives a direct path.
{
    ?x :edge ?y
} => {
    ?x :path ?y
} .

# Extend a known path by one edge. Repeated pairs add no new fact, so
# closure stops even though the graph contains a cycle.
{
    ?x :path ?y .
    ?y :edge ?z
} => {
    ?x :path ?z
} .
